WEBVTT

00:11.910 --> 00:17.830
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

01:30.360 --> 01:34.740
#50: THE ANONYMOUS (ASININE) A-TEAM
AND A CRISIS

01:37.240 --> 01:42.370
Silvi, we said we'd start training
first thing in the morning.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.000
It's past noon now.
Care to explain yourself?

01:46.390 --> 01:50.300
Well... I started to see
why the game was so legendary.

01:50.300 --> 01:52.800
I got so caught up in it,
I forgot to log out!

01:52.800 --> 01:55.300
Didn't she say she was turning in early?

01:55.300 --> 01:57.640
I knew she was playing another game.

01:58.021 --> 01:59.607
Order, please!

02:00.060 --> 02:00.810
STEAK 500G×4

02:00.810 --> 02:01.770
MEDIUM

02:01.770 --> 02:02.770
RARE

02:02.770 --> 02:03.730
RARE (LOTS OF GARLIC)

02:03.730 --> 02:05.060
WELL DONE (LOTS OF GARLIC)

02:06.610 --> 02:08.110
I'm just going to make sure.

02:08.110 --> 02:09.820
You're eating all that by yourself?

02:10.690 --> 02:11.820
You bet!

02:11.820 --> 02:15.320
I gotta get my calories in for training!

02:16.160 --> 02:18.410
You're always such a glutton.

02:18.410 --> 02:20.580
Still, hard to believe you just woke up.

02:22.210 --> 02:23.160
That's right.

02:23.160 --> 02:27.840
Team Nitro Squad, our opponent tomorrow,
has posted their lineup.

02:28.920 --> 02:30.760
Why bother looking?

02:30.760 --> 02:32.340
K's the one who matters.

02:32.840 --> 02:36.340
Actually, there's something here
that might catch your interest.

02:37.220 --> 02:40.152
Two totally unknown players.

02:40.720 --> 02:43.730
4 DAYS UNTIL X-DAY

02:43.730 --> 02:46.230
I'm sorry! I slept late!

02:49.270 --> 02:52.740
Umm... By the way,
I'm pretty hungry...

02:52.740 --> 02:56.700
You think you're in a position to make
demands after making us wait this long?

02:56.700 --> 02:58.858
I was wondering
what was taking you so long.

02:58.860 --> 03:00.240
Can't believe you were still asleep.

03:00.830 --> 03:03.080
Sorry, but we don't have time to waste.

03:03.080 --> 03:04.460
You can eat after this.

03:07.040 --> 03:07.934
If you want.

03:10.000 --> 03:11.710
- Natsume always delivers!

03:11.710 --> 03:13.130
- But before we can discuss
- Natsume always delivers!

03:13.130 --> 03:14.300
- about strats against Team USA,
- Natsume always delivers!

03:14.300 --> 03:16.930
- there's something else we need to do.
- But wait, how am I supposed to eat it?

03:16.930 --> 03:18.010
What's that?

03:18.010 --> 03:20.510
Register our lineup.

03:20.510 --> 03:24.060
The entry deadline is at noon today.

03:24.060 --> 03:26.390
Me and Meg have done it already...

03:26.843 --> 03:27.770
But you guys haven't, right?

03:27.770 --> 03:28.270
NITRO SQUAD
But you guys haven't, right?

03:28.270 --> 03:29.110
NITRO SQUAD

03:29.110 --> 03:31.860
You can just put whatever for my name.

03:31.860 --> 03:34.110
Are you okay putting your name
and face out there?

03:34.110 --> 03:36.570
No way, I'm totally gonna hide them.

03:37.320 --> 03:41.580
It might be a bit much for
today's teens to handle!

03:42.490 --> 03:46.865
Yeah, celebrity model Towa Amane
participating in a gaming tournament...

03:46.870 --> 03:49.080
It'd definitely generate buzz.

03:49.580 --> 03:53.000
And her work would dry up if people
found out what she's really like.

03:54.460 --> 03:57.130
Sunraku, you're gonna
keep hiding your face?

03:57.800 --> 03:59.840
Not sure...

04:00.470 --> 04:03.180
I don't wanna show my face at the match.

04:03.180 --> 04:07.850
But it feels a little weird
participating like this...

04:07.850 --> 04:10.440
About that, Sunraku.

04:11.520 --> 04:15.400
If you're gonna hide your face either way,
how about we cosplay together?

04:18.360 --> 04:24.370
It makes way more sense to go
in full costume than to hide just my face!

04:24.370 --> 04:28.410
That's why I ordered
a costume just yesterday!

04:28.410 --> 04:30.225
You work fast!

04:30.230 --> 04:32.500
It should arrive today!

04:32.500 --> 04:34.050
Delivery's fast!

04:34.050 --> 04:37.920
And I tagged on a costume
for you in there too!

04:37.920 --> 04:41.470
"Tagged on," my butt!
I never asked you for that!

04:41.470 --> 04:45.390
You think you can nix my ideas when you
can't even make it to meetings on time?!

04:46.180 --> 04:49.310
It'll look way better on you
than that gas mask.

04:49.310 --> 04:51.060
I'll drop it off later.

04:51.060 --> 04:54.110
How often do you get a celebrity model
putting together your outfit, anyway?

04:54.570 --> 04:57.690
B-By the way, what will you be wearing?

04:58.072 --> 05:01.950
You'll just have to wait and see!

05:04.450 --> 05:06.870
How can you guys be so laid-back?!

05:06.870 --> 05:08.960
Do you understand
how important this event is?!

05:08.960 --> 05:11.960
This is a seriously big match, darn it!

05:12.460 --> 05:14.340
But it's basically
a big party, right?

05:14.340 --> 05:16.130
We've gotta have fun!

05:16.130 --> 05:19.621
And being a pro is about
putting on a good show, right?

05:20.858 --> 05:21.930
Geez!

05:21.930 --> 05:23.640
Fine, I get it.

05:23.640 --> 05:26.890
Are we good with Sunraku
and Pencil Knight for names?

05:26.890 --> 05:29.640
Nah, let's do something new
for the big event.

05:30.230 --> 05:32.400
Let's see...

05:32.400 --> 05:36.440
Sunraku can be "Mortar Ration"
and Pencilgon can be "Ringmaster"

05:36.440 --> 05:38.400
Did you just call me cannon fodder?!

05:38.400 --> 05:41.450
And I'm not running this show, you are!

05:41.869 --> 05:44.950
Maybe we should ask Meg
to pick our names!

05:44.950 --> 05:46.490
What? Me?

05:47.370 --> 05:50.080
You're really putting me on the spot...

05:50.750 --> 05:55.880
Someone who wants to hide their face
and someone who wants to hide their name...

05:55.880 --> 05:57.090
NITRO SQUAD
No Face and No Name?

05:57.090 --> 05:58.710
No Face and No Name?

05:58.710 --> 06:01.630
Last-minute ringers, huh?

06:02.090 --> 06:06.300
Well, I'd heard that a few of their
members couldn't participate.

06:06.300 --> 06:10.520
Whoever they are,
they can't be better than K.

06:10.930 --> 06:15.060
You're right. K's the one
we have to worry about.

06:15.060 --> 06:17.820
I've really been waiting for this.

06:18.570 --> 06:20.860
Don't disappoint me, now...

06:21.400 --> 06:23.070
Okay, K?

06:23.950 --> 06:26.280
So, regarding our strategy...

06:27.620 --> 06:28.120
BOSS

06:28.120 --> 06:29.410
BOSS
From my manager?

06:29.410 --> 06:30.120
BOSS

06:31.330 --> 06:32.620
Yes? K speaking.

06:33.040 --> 06:33.710
Yes.

06:34.210 --> 06:35.630
No, it's fine.

06:36.920 --> 06:38.000
Yeah...

06:39.340 --> 06:40.170
What?!

06:40.630 --> 06:43.630
W-Wait, why do I have to—

06:43.630 --> 06:46.180
You're kidding, right?
You better be—

06:46.720 --> 06:48.550
No way! Hang on a—

06:49.720 --> 06:51.020
The jerk hung up...

06:51.352 --> 06:53.061
What's wrong?

06:56.060 --> 06:58.400
For the match tomorrow...

07:00.690 --> 07:03.650
I'm not gonna be able to be there.

07:06.410 --> 07:08.910
What?!

07:08.910 --> 07:10.660
Wh-What do you mean?

07:10.660 --> 07:12.910
Orders from a sponsor.

07:12.910 --> 07:19.540
They volunteered me to fill a slot for
a different game tournament tomorrow.

07:20.500 --> 07:22.630
What game is that?

07:23.050 --> 07:26.800
The Ruins War Hounds 6
world championships.

07:26.800 --> 07:29.970
They want me in the finals.

07:30.390 --> 07:33.520
But doesn't that team
have its own alternates?

07:33.520 --> 07:36.100
Apparently, they all got food poisoning.

07:36.100 --> 07:38.810
What in the world
were those idiots eating?!

07:39.272 --> 07:41.980
What's this Ruins War thing again?

07:41.980 --> 07:44.400
Pretty sure it's an FPS.

07:44.400 --> 07:45.650
That's right!

07:45.650 --> 07:49.120
But why would they ask for you,
a fighting game player?

07:49.527 --> 07:53.990
I played an FPS in front
of the sponsor before.

07:53.990 --> 07:56.830
It's my next best genre
after fighting games.

07:57.250 --> 08:00.960
I guess I ended up showboating a little...

08:00.960 --> 08:02.670
I get it.

08:02.670 --> 08:05.880
And because you showed off
like a dummy, they picked you.

08:06.300 --> 08:09.140
For a world championship, at that.

08:09.140 --> 08:12.010
Your own fame was your undoing.

08:12.850 --> 08:14.810
Looks like it.

08:14.810 --> 08:20.298
And since it's a direct order from a sponsor,
your organization can't say no.

08:21.310 --> 08:23.900
An exhibition versus
a world championships...

08:23.900 --> 08:26.780
Ours is just fun and games by comparison.

08:27.163 --> 08:29.780
According to tomorrow's schedule,

08:29.780 --> 08:34.160
the Ruins War Hounds 6 championship
starts tomorrow at nine.

08:34.700 --> 08:38.160
Our exhibition match starts at ten.

08:38.160 --> 08:39.920
So we've got an hour?

08:40.460 --> 08:44.380
How long does this
Ruins War Hounds thing take to play?

08:44.380 --> 08:47.550
It'll be five matches,
about thirty minutes each.

08:47.550 --> 08:50.380
With breaks,
I'll be tied down for three hours.

08:51.300 --> 08:54.720
I'll be going two hours over
no matter what happens.

08:56.890 --> 09:00.940
We're down to the wire,
and now Kei can't compete?

09:01.400 --> 09:02.810
What will we do?

09:03.207 --> 09:04.690
I think he can make it.

09:06.650 --> 09:09.490
The exhibition match
uses a knockout format.

09:09.490 --> 09:13.660
We'll just make Katzo our anchor,
the last one to play.

09:14.240 --> 09:18.000
We can bet Silvi's gonna
be their anchor too.

09:19.620 --> 09:22.420
The time limit for each round
is ten minutes.

09:22.420 --> 09:24.170
The first to win two rounds wins the match.

09:24.840 --> 09:28.460
So if we let our opponent
take one round,

09:28.460 --> 09:31.930
and make all three rounds
run the full time limit...

09:32.360 --> 09:34.430
Each match will end up
being thirty minutes.

09:35.350 --> 09:38.060
If we manipulate things
so we win and lose one match,

09:38.487 --> 09:41.560
there'll be six matches before
the anchors play each other.

09:41.560 --> 09:46.070
In other words, we could theoretically
drag things out to 180 minutes.

09:46.690 --> 09:49.112
You could squeak in then, right?

09:50.240 --> 09:53.910
Fight three rounds,
letting them all run to the time limit?

09:53.910 --> 09:56.370
Manipulate things
so we win and lose one match?

09:56.370 --> 09:58.410
W-What are you talking about?

09:58.410 --> 10:04.040
You think you can arrange things that
easily against the USA's top team?!

10:04.040 --> 10:06.250
I'm just talking theoretically.

10:06.250 --> 10:11.920
Any time we lose, you can make up
for it if you get back fast enough.

10:11.920 --> 10:13.510
Come on, man.

10:13.510 --> 10:18.600
We're facing a powerhouse German team
that won their way to the world finals!

10:18.600 --> 10:20.680
Just beating them will be
hard enough and you—

10:20.680 --> 10:21.600
Katzo.

10:22.560 --> 10:25.190
The question you should be asking
isn't whether it's possible.

10:25.770 --> 10:27.900
It's how you're gonna make it happen.

10:29.730 --> 10:34.610
If you just give up on that,
you won't get to fight Sylvia.

10:37.530 --> 10:39.790
At least, that's how I see things.

10:39.790 --> 10:41.450
What do you think, Pencilgon?

10:43.330 --> 10:45.670
During the Wethermon fight,

10:46.170 --> 10:51.960
I planned our strategy around you,
Sunraku, as our sword.

10:52.590 --> 10:57.140
For this, we'll all have to be swords.

10:57.140 --> 10:59.010
In other words, it's a multi-sword style.

11:00.510 --> 11:05.020
If even one of us breaks,
any plan I make goes up in smoke.

11:05.770 --> 11:11.570
Quite frankly, a plan to beat the US team
with just the three of us would be easier.

11:12.570 --> 11:16.360
What you're proposing is basically
trolling the US's top team.

11:19.030 --> 11:19.780
But...

11:20.280 --> 11:22.700
There's a way to do it.

11:25.960 --> 11:27.830
Sunraku, you said earlier.

11:27.830 --> 11:31.130
An exhibition match is
"fun and games," right?

11:31.461 --> 11:34.938
In other words, it's entertainment.

11:35.781 --> 11:38.720
Entertainment?

11:38.720 --> 11:41.310
If we can take advantage of that...

11:41.850 --> 11:44.930
We could get ourselves that 180 minutes.

11:47.230 --> 11:51.860
It's something I can do, too, right?

11:51.860 --> 11:53.440
Of course.

11:53.440 --> 11:56.150
It wouldn't be a good plan otherwise.

11:57.240 --> 11:58.410
All right.

11:58.860 --> 12:00.200
I'll play along, then.

12:00.669 --> 12:01.909
Meg?

12:02.310 --> 12:03.643
Sounds like we've agreed.

12:04.200 --> 12:05.913
What about you, Katzo?

12:06.334 --> 12:07.750
You guys...

12:07.750 --> 12:11.920
You really think we can
work through this disaster?

12:12.327 --> 12:14.050
Oh, c'mon.

12:14.050 --> 12:17.420
We run into stuff like this
in games every day.

12:18.130 --> 12:22.276
Conquering adversity is what
gamers like us do, right?

12:24.680 --> 12:25.980
(AUTO-TRANSLATE) I'M LOOKING FORWARD
TO A REMATCH WITH YOU.

12:25.980 --> 12:27.020
MY "METEORS" WILL BEAT YOUR "LAVA" AGAIN
AT THE NEXT GGC.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.270
I see.

12:34.070 --> 12:35.320
That's right.

12:35.780 --> 12:37.740
K-Kei?

12:38.450 --> 12:42.160
Sorry. The unexpected glitch
had me panicking a little.

12:42.160 --> 12:44.030
Guess I've got a lot to learn.

12:45.490 --> 12:47.290
Sunraku's right.

12:48.330 --> 12:52.460
Even if I can't solve this myself,
I'm not alone.

12:53.290 --> 12:56.550
I can put my faith in Meg and these two.

12:57.800 --> 13:01.010
Mind explaining your plan, Pencilgon?

13:01.840 --> 13:02.930
Certainly.

13:03.490 --> 13:06.060
In that case...

13:06.465 --> 13:07.930
Let's get scheming.

13:22.778 --> 13:24.410
From Katzo?

13:24.410 --> 13:27.910
There better not be some new issue...

13:27.910 --> 13:29.663
FROM: MODOR KATZO - TO: SUNRAKU
WHY ARE YOU DOING ALL THIS FOR ME?

13:30.029 --> 13:31.870
Why, he asks?

13:34.380 --> 13:39.170
This whole thing was serious enough
that you invited us, right?

13:39.630 --> 13:43.510
I said I was gonna help you
look good, dummy.

13:43.510 --> 13:45.527
If it goes well,
let's go out for yakiniku.

13:45.530 --> 13:47.236
On your tab, of course.

13:51.803 --> 13:56.690
The match with Sylvia
is important to you, right?

13:57.150 --> 14:00.440
Big sister here is giving
the shirt off her back to help you!

14:00.990 --> 14:04.700
Well, my costume will have a shirt,
more or less...

14:04.700 --> 14:07.620
If it all goes well,
I'd sure love to eat some sushi!

14:07.620 --> 14:10.000
Your treat, of course.

14:10.000 --> 14:13.790
They're gonna take me for all I'm worth.

14:13.790 --> 14:17.710
And I'm already paying their hotel fees...

14:18.210 --> 14:22.380
I was feeling pretty lousy
when my boss gave me that order...

14:23.090 --> 14:26.850
But now, I'm excited as hell.

14:27.470 --> 14:29.720
Wait for me, guys.

14:29.720 --> 14:33.520
I'll beat that other team
and get right back to you!

14:33.980 --> 14:37.980
4 DAYS UNTIL X-DAY

14:38.980 --> 14:41.490
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

14:41.990 --> 14:43.490
4 DAYS UNTIL X-DAY

14:43.490 --> 14:46.990
DAY OF THE EXHIBITION MATCH

14:46.990 --> 14:49.490
GLOBAL GAME COMPETITION VENUE

14:58.090 --> 15:00.590
Silvi's third?!

15:00.590 --> 15:02.670
Unexpected, right?

15:03.170 --> 15:07.300
Our plan assumed Sylvia would go fourth.

15:08.510 --> 15:12.890
We're gonna need
to cut some time off the plan.

15:12.890 --> 15:17.560
How fast do I have to win
the Ruins War Hounds 6 match now?!

15:18.360 --> 15:22.070
It means the rest of us can't
afford mistakes, either.

15:22.070 --> 15:25.240
Just means the difficulty level's
gone from hard to very hard.

15:25.240 --> 15:28.700
We knew from the start that
it wouldn't be easy, right?

15:29.240 --> 15:31.240
That's what our preparations were for.

15:33.120 --> 15:34.540
You're right.

15:34.540 --> 15:38.670
The only thing each of us
can do is give it our best.

15:39.210 --> 15:40.000
Yeah!

15:40.000 --> 15:41.670
Fine.

15:41.670 --> 15:45.630
But are you guys really gonna
compete in those outfits?

15:45.630 --> 15:47.260
Of course, we are!

15:47.260 --> 15:49.720
That's part of the plan.

15:50.850 --> 15:53.430
C'mon, it'll make it feel
like a real event.

15:53.430 --> 15:56.640
Nobody's stopped me from wearing this to the event hall,

15:56.640 --> 15:59.400
so I guess it's a "costumes welcome" thing?

16:01.060 --> 16:04.650
That's right. I wanted to
give you something, Sunraku.

16:06.458 --> 16:08.910
Riot Blood made in the USA!

16:08.910 --> 16:10.950
You kidding me?!

16:10.950 --> 16:13.910
I can't believe you got me the real thing!

16:14.334 --> 16:18.540
And it's the newest in the lineup,
Riot Blood Tonight!

16:18.540 --> 16:23.800
It's the best energy drink that's set
millions of energy drink users quaking!

16:23.800 --> 16:25.760
Whoa!

16:26.550 --> 16:29.050
- They're calling me in.
- Got me a Tonight!

16:29.930 --> 16:32.300
I guess I'd better get going.

16:32.300 --> 16:34.430
No worries, Katzo.

16:34.930 --> 16:39.767
We'll make sure you get your turn.

16:41.060 --> 16:42.980
Go kick some ass!

16:45.110 --> 16:49.780
Sure. And then I'll do the same
in Galaxia Heroes: Chaos.

16:53.200 --> 16:55.160
EXHIBITION MATCH

16:55.160 --> 16:57.200
EXHIBITION MATCH
Attention, everyone!

16:57.200 --> 17:01.460
We're about to start
the Galaxia Heroes: Chaos

17:01.460 --> 17:05.880
game demonstration
and special exhibition match!

17:08.720 --> 17:13.350
Galaxia Heroes: Chaos was developed
with technologies provided by

17:13.350 --> 17:17.680
Utopia Entertainment Software,
the makers of Shangri-La Frontier,

17:17.680 --> 17:20.230
and is thus a new evolution of the series!

17:20.640 --> 17:25.047
It's the long-awaited second
SLF-generation title!

17:26.101 --> 17:30.280
What kind of battles will we see?!

17:31.320 --> 17:34.200
I'll be your MC and play-by-play announcer,

17:34.200 --> 17:37.160
EIGHT SASAHARA
Eight Sasahara!

17:37.160 --> 17:39.870
EIGHT SASAHARA

17:39.870 --> 17:48.170
And on color commentary, we have Ayato Asama
from the pro gaming team Colt Bison!

17:48.170 --> 17:51.010
COLT BISON - AYATO ASAMA
I'm afraid I don't play enough fighting games

17:51.010 --> 17:52.720
COLT BISON - AYATO ASAMA
to provide adequate commentary...

17:52.720 --> 17:55.762
COLT BISON - AYATO ASAMA
But thank you for having me.

17:59.350 --> 18:04.270
Now, let's bring on the players!

18:07.440 --> 18:12.225
From the American esports
organization Zodiac Cluster,

18:12.230 --> 18:15.410
led by the USA's number one player,
Sylvia Goldberg,

18:15.410 --> 18:18.830
their fighting game arm... Star Rain!

18:21.500 --> 18:23.250
Sylvia Goldberg!

18:23.250 --> 18:24.620
Lucas Garcia!

18:24.620 --> 18:26.130
Alex Taylor!

18:26.130 --> 18:28.800
Johnson Sean Underwood!

18:30.170 --> 18:31.090
- Silvi!

18:31.090 --> 18:32.050
- Johnson! Crush an apple in one hand!
- Silvi!

18:32.050 --> 18:33.430
- Johnson! Crush an apple in one hand!
- Lucas!

18:33.430 --> 18:34.550
- Johnson! Crush an apple in one hand!
- Hey, Alex! You've got wings! Macho man!

18:34.550 --> 18:36.350
- Hey, Alex! You've got wings! Macho man!

18:36.350 --> 18:40.640
Star Rain has amassed
an incredible record this year,

18:40.640 --> 18:44.520
winning six out of the eight
tournaments they've participated in.

18:44.520 --> 18:46.860
No one could deny they're a top team.

18:46.860 --> 18:48.440
I see!

18:48.440 --> 18:49.860
And most of all...

18:50.530 --> 18:54.516
Silvi herself remains undefeated.

18:54.516 --> 18:54.520
Silvi herself remains undefeated.
I-Incredible!
A rare undisputed champion!

18:54.520 --> 18:58.120
I-Incredible!
A rare undisputed champion!

18:59.200 --> 19:01.950
Now, who faces these tough opponents?!

19:02.830 --> 19:07.040
From the Japanese esports
organization Cyber Battalion,

19:07.040 --> 19:12.050
their fighting game arm led by
Japan's pride and joy, the genius K,

19:12.480 --> 19:14.090
it's Nitro Squad!

19:15.880 --> 19:18.140
- Kei!
- Been waiting for you, Kei!

19:18.140 --> 19:19.220
Kei!

19:19.220 --> 19:23.180
Due to various circumstances,
they'll be taking on two alternates...

19:26.100 --> 19:27.520
Hey, you kidding me?

19:27.520 --> 19:29.940
Now, is everybody ready?

19:29.940 --> 19:34.280
It's time for our entertainment show!

19:37.780 --> 19:40.530
W-What in the world is happening?!

19:40.530 --> 19:42.160
Nitro Squad...

19:42.160 --> 19:47.420
Its members are K, No Face,
No Name, and Nu2meg!

19:47.920 --> 19:50.420
What a unique-looking team!

19:50.920 --> 19:52.590
An unknown quantity.

19:52.590 --> 19:54.276
I don't know what to make of them.

19:59.640 --> 20:02.680
I love this!

20:05.600 --> 20:08.940
Typical celebrity.
She knows how to command a stage.

20:08.940 --> 20:14.400
Do I look weird right now,
as the only one not in a costume?

20:14.400 --> 20:18.570
If you're that worried,
you could've cosplayed too, Natsume.

20:18.570 --> 20:20.320
No freaking way!

20:20.320 --> 20:21.990
What in the world?

20:21.990 --> 20:25.160
When did Nitro Squad
become a cosplay group?

20:25.160 --> 20:26.960
That pumpkin-head guy...

20:26.960 --> 20:30.460
Isn't he from that FPS,
Requiem For Armies?

20:33.920 --> 20:36.510
Sunraku, you will play the character

20:36.510 --> 20:40.470
who sometimes hinders the protagonist,
sometimes fights beside him,

20:40.870 --> 20:44.890
and in the end disappears into
the ocean's depths with a nuclear bomb...

20:44.890 --> 20:50.100
His true face unknown to all,
the faceless mercenary Jack!

20:50.530 --> 20:53.150
That's the story behind your costume.

20:53.150 --> 20:56.490
Perfect for "No Face" right?

20:56.490 --> 20:59.820
Seems a little early
for Halloween, though...

20:59.820 --> 21:02.570
And what's your costume?

21:05.080 --> 21:08.080
Protecting the castle of
a doomed country to the death,

21:08.080 --> 21:12.880
the lady knight of Silent Grace, Nameless!

21:18.970 --> 21:22.550
So, they are "No Face" and "No Name"?

21:22.550 --> 21:24.600
I like it. It's fun!

21:25.390 --> 21:27.810
But... there's no Kei?

21:31.650 --> 21:33.940
Now that both teams are here...

21:34.980 --> 21:40.030
Huh? Nitro Squad,
are you missing a member?

21:40.490 --> 21:41.941
Where's Kei?

21:42.894 --> 21:44.530
Rest easy.

21:44.530 --> 21:46.990
He'll be here...

21:46.990 --> 21:49.040
...to beat you.

21:51.410 --> 21:56.130
Umm... So he's running late?

21:56.130 --> 21:59.090
He's fighting a brutal battle
in the bathroom.

21:59.090 --> 22:00.840
Just go on without him.

22:01.420 --> 22:02.800
R-Right.

22:03.550 --> 22:06.720
Then let me officially explain the rules.

22:06.720 --> 22:10.060
This is a simple knockout tournament!

22:10.060 --> 22:12.940
The battle stage will be Chaos City!

22:12.940 --> 22:18.940
Cube victory and NPC civilians
will both be turned on!

22:21.740 --> 22:27.580
Now, the Galaxia Heroes: Chaos
special exhibition match...

22:27.970 --> 22:31.000
Star Rain versus Nitro Squad shall begin!

22:31.000 --> 22:32.710
NITRO SQUAD
Star Rain versus Nitro Squad shall begin!

22:37.210 --> 22:41.460
The lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome;

22:41.460 --> 22:44.470
celebrity model Towa Amane;

22:44.470 --> 22:47.180
and professional gamer Megumi Natsume...

22:48.220 --> 22:54.100
Will they be able to hold out
until Kei arrives?

22:54.980 --> 23:01.110
And will Sunraku be able
to defeat the unique monster,

23:01.110 --> 23:05.240
Ctarnidd of the Abyss,
in Shangri-La Frontier?

23:11.290 --> 23:13.120
It goes down on X-Day.

23:14.000 --> 23:16.000
Abyssal time draws ever nearer.

23:16.000 --> 23:18.880
ABYSSAL TIME
Abyssal time draws ever nearer.

23:18.880 --> 23:23.880
ABYSSAL TIME
